# Ironforged Clan Events — Plugin Hub rules

Follow `AGENTS.md` in this repo (from RuneLite’s example-plugin). Hard constraints below.

## Never ship

- Reflection, JNI/JNA, ProcessBuilder, serialization, dynamic code loading
- Client-thread network/disk IO; prefer OkHttp `enqueue()` or executor + `execute()`
- `new Gson()` — always `@Inject Gson`
- `HttpURLConnection` / `java.net.http` — always `@Inject OkHttpClient`
- `Desktop.browse` — use `LinkBrowser`
- Dead/unused classes, seasonal/reporter stacks, or unused `data/` in the JAR
- Oversized PNGs (keep nav/hub icons ≤48px; prefer 16–32 for nav)
- `META-INF/services/net.runelite.client.plugins.Plugin`
- New third-party Gradle deps without hub verification metadata (avoid unless required)

## Third-party networking

Any feature that contacts a non-RuneLite server must be:

1. **Opt-in** (default off)
2. Annotated with exact warning:  
   `"This feature submits your IP address to a 3rd-party server not controlled or verified by RuneLite developers"`

Google Sheets uses `enableGoogleSheets` for this. Do not fetch when it is false.

## Config

- Keep group id specific: `ironforgedclanevents`
- Do not rename keys/groups without a migration
- Do not mix pure reformat commits with feature changes

## Packaging before PR

- `runelite-plugin.properties` displayName/tags/plugins match the plugin
- Root `icon.png` ≤48×72
- `settings.gradle` project name set (not `example`)
- Java 11 (`options.release.set(11)`)
- BSD-2 LICENSE present
- Clean `shutDown()` removes overlays/nav/subscriptions
- README describes user-facing features only (no dead seasonal docs)

## Testing

Do not automate RuneScape input. Offer `./gradlew.bat runClient`, tell the user what to verify, wait for confirmation.
